# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Pendahuluan {#introduction}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a chemist runs an NMR experiment, they place a sample of nuclear spins in a strong magnetic field, apply a radio-frequency (RF) pulse, and measure the signal that comes back. The technique rests on a few ideas from the quantum mechanics of a spin-1/2 particle in a magnetic field. The spin has two energy levels separated by an energy that corresponds to a characteristic Larmor frequency. A resonant pulse at that frequency tips the spin into the transverse plane, where it precesses and induces a signal that then fades with two characteristic times, $T_1$ and $T_2$.\n"
msgstr "Ketika seorang kimiawan menjalankan eksperimen NMR, mereka menaruh sampel spin nuklir dalam medan magnet kuat, menerapkan pulsa radio-frequency (RF), lalu mengukur sinyal yang kembali. Teknik ini bertumpu pada beberapa ide dari mekanika kuantum partikel spin-1/2 dalam medan magnet. Spin punya dua level energi yang dipisahkan oleh energi yang sesuai dengan frekuensi Larmor tertentu. Pulsa resonan pada frekuensi itu membuat spin miring ke bidang transversal, di mana ia berpresesi dan menginduksi sinyal yang kemudian meluruh dengan dua waktu karakteristik, $T_1$ dan $T_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A superconducting **qubit** is an engineered version of the same object: a controllable two-level quantum system. Its $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ states are the analog of spin-up and spin-down, the gate we apply to rotate it is the analog of the RF pulse, and it loses coherence with its own $T_1$ and $T_2$. This is not merely a loose comparison; some of the earliest experimental quantum processors in the late 1990s and early 2000s used NMR.\n"
msgstr "**Qubit** superkonduktor adalah versi rekayasa dari objek yang sama: sistem kuantum dua level yang bisa dikendalikan. State $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$-nya adalah analog dari spin-up dan spin-down, gate yang kita terapkan untuk memutarnya adalah analog dari pulsa RF, dan ia kehilangan koherensi dengan $T_1$ dan $T_2$-nya sendiri. Ini bukan sekadar perbandingan longgar; beberapa prosesor kuantum eksperimental paling awal pada akhir 1990-an dan awal 2000-an memakai NMR.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this module you will use a real quantum computer to run the same characterization experiments that an NMR spectroscopist (or a quantum engineer calibrating hardware) performs:\n"
msgstr "Di modul ini kamu akan memakai komputer kuantum sungguhan untuk menjalankan eksperimen karakterisasi yang sama dengan yang dilakukan seorang spektroskopis NMR (atau insinyur kuantum yang mengkalibrasi hardware):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Rabi / nutation** — driving the spin and watching it rotate. This is how you calibrate a $\\pi$ or $\\pi/2$ rotation.\n"
msgstr "**Rabi / nutasi** — menggerakkan spin dan mengamatinya berputar. Beginilah cara mengkalibrasi rotasi $\\pi$ atau $\\pi/2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_1$** — spin-lattice relaxation, the decay of an excited spin back to equilibrium.\n"
msgstr "**$T_1$** — relaksasi spin-kisi, peluruhan spin tereksitasi kembali ke kesetimbangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_2$** — spin-spin relaxation (dephasing), measured with a Ramsey experiment and refocused with a Hahn echo.\n"
msgstr "**$T_2$** — relaksasi spin-spin (dephasing), diukur dengan eksperimen Ramsey dan difokus ulang dengan Hahn echo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NMR spectroscopy (chemical shift and $J$-coupling)** — simulating a small molecule on several qubits and reading its multiplet spectrum to recover connectivity through the $n+1$ rule.\n"
msgstr "**Spektroskopi NMR (pergeseran kimia dan kopling $J$)** — mensimulasikan molekul kecil pada beberapa qubit dan membaca spektrum multipletnya untuk mendapatkan kembali konektivitas melalui aturan $n+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each concept we first give the minimal theory, then implement the experiment in Qiskit following the four-step *Qiskit patterns* workflow.\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap konsep, pertama-tama kita berikan teori minimalnya, lalu mengimplementasikan eksperimennya di Qiskit mengikuti alur kerja empat langkah *Qiskit patterns*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory}"
msgstr "Teori {#theory}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-1/2 particles in a magnetic field {#spin-12-particles-in-a-magnetic-field}"
msgstr "Partikel spin-1/2 dalam medan magnet {#spin-12-particles-in-a-magnetic-field}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A spin-1/2 nucleus has a magnetic moment $\\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\gamma \\hbar \\mathbf{I}$, where $\\gamma$ is the gyromagnetic ratio. In a static field $B_0$ along $z$, the two spin states split in energy (the **Zeeman effect**):\n"
msgstr "Inti atom spin-1/2 punya momen magnetik $\\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\gamma \\hbar \\mathbf{I}$, dengan $\\gamma$ adalah rasio giromagnetik. Dalam medan statis $B_0$ sepanjang $z$, kedua state spin terpecah dalam energi (**efek Zeeman**):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$E_{\\pm} = \\mp \\tfrac{1}{2}\\gamma \\hbar B_0, \\qquad \\Delta E = \\gamma \\hbar B_0 = \\hbar \\omega_0 .$$\n"
msgstr "$$E_{\\pm} = \\mp \\tfrac{1}{2}\\gamma \\hbar B_0, \\qquad \\Delta E = \\gamma \\hbar B_0 = \\hbar \\omega_0 .$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The energy gap defines the **Larmor (resonance) frequency** $\\omega_0 = \\gamma B_0$. The magnetic moment **precesses** about $B_0$ at this same frequency.\n"
msgstr "Celah energi ini mendefinisikan **frekuensi Larmor (resonansi)** $\\omega_0 = \\gamma B_0$. Momen magnetik **berpresesi** mengelilingi $B_0$ pada frekuensi yang sama ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To rotate the spin we apply an oscillating RF field at (or near) $\\omega_0$. In the frame rotating at the drive frequency (the **rotating frame**), a resonant drive rotates the Bloch vector about an axis in the $x$-$y$ plane. How far it rotates (the **flip angle**) is set by the pulse's strength and duration. Two choices matter most: a $90^\\circ$ pulse tips a $+1/2$ spin into the transverse plane, and a $180^\\circ$ pulse rotates it fully to $-1/2$.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memutar spin, kita menerapkan medan RF berosilasi pada (atau dekat) $\\omega_0$. Dalam kerangka yang berputar pada frekuensi drive (**rotating frame**), drive resonan memutar vektor Bloch mengelilingi sumbu di bidang $x$-$y$. Seberapa jauh ia berputar (**flip angle**) ditentukan oleh kekuatan dan durasi pulsa. Dua pilihan yang paling penting: pulsa $90^\\circ$ memiringkan spin $+1/2$ ke bidang transversal, dan pulsa $180^\\circ$ memutarnya penuh ke $-1/2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Translating between NMR and quantum computing jargon {#translating-between-nmr-and-quantum-computing-jargon}"
msgstr "Menerjemahkan antara jargon NMR dan komputasi kuantum {#translating-between-nmr-and-quantum-computing-jargon}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit is a two-level system, mathematically identical to a spin-1/2 in a magnetic field &mdash; so while we're running on a quantum processor rather than a nucleus, the physics is the same physics that underlies NMR. Only the vocabulary differs. This table helps you talk to physical chemists and quantum-computing specialists alike.\n"
msgstr "Qubit adalah sistem dua level, secara matematis identik dengan spin-1/2 dalam medan magnet &mdash; jadi meskipun kita berjalan di prosesor kuantum dan bukan di inti atom, fisikanya adalah fisika yang sama yang mendasari NMR. Hanya kosakatanya yang berbeda. Tabel ini membantumu berkomunikasi dengan kimiawan fisika maupun spesialis komputasi kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| NMR / spin-1/2 | Quantum processor (qubit) |\n"
"| ---|---|\n"
"| Spin-up / spin-down | $\\ket{0}$ / $\\ket{1}$ |\n"
"| Zeeman gap $\\Delta E = \\hbar\\omega_0$ | Qubit transition energy $\\hbar\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Larmor frequency $\\omega_0$ | Qubit frequency $\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Resonant RF pulse (flip angle $\\theta$) | Single-qubit rotation gate $R_X(\\theta)$ |\n"
"| $90^\\circ$ / $180^\\circ$ pulse | $R_X(\\pi/2)$ / $R_X(\\pi)$ |\n"
"| Spin-lattice relaxation $T_1$ | Qubit energy-relaxation time $T_1$ |\n"
"| Spin-spin relaxation $T_2$ | Qubit dephasing time $T_2$ |\n"
"| Nutation | Rabi oscillations |\n"
"| Free induction decay (FID), Hahn echo | Ramsey, echo sequences |\n"
msgstr ""
"| NMR / spin-1/2 | Prosesor kuantum (qubit) |\n"
"| ---|---|\n"
"| Spin-up / spin-down | $\\ket{0}$ / $\\ket{1}$ |\n"
"| Celah Zeeman $\\Delta E = \\hbar\\omega_0$ | Energi transisi qubit $\\hbar\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Frekuensi Larmor $\\omega_0$ | Frekuensi qubit $\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Pulsa RF resonan (flip angle $\\theta$) | Gate rotasi single-qubit $R_X(\\theta)$ |\n"
"| Pulsa $90^\\circ$ / $180^\\circ$ | $R_X(\\pi/2)$ / $R_X(\\pi)$ |\n"
"| Relaksasi spin-kisi $T_1$ | Waktu relaksasi energi qubit $T_1$ |\n"
"| Relaksasi spin-spin $T_2$ | Waktu dephasing qubit $T_2$ |\n"
"| Nutasi | Osilasi Rabi |\n"
"| Free induction decay (FID), Hahn echo | Urutan Ramsey, echo |\n"

