# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experiment: Rabi oscillations (nutation) {#experiment-rabi-oscillations-nutation}"
msgstr "Eksperimen: osilasi Rabi (nutasi) {#experiment-rabi-oscillations-nutation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory-1}"
msgstr "Teori {#theory-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drive a spin on resonance and its Bloch vector rotates steadily from pole to pole &mdash; it **nutates**. If we apply a rotation of flip angle $\\theta$ about the $x$-axis to a qubit starting in $|0\\rangle$, the probability of finding it in $|1\\rangle$ is:\n"
msgstr "Gerakkan spin pada resonansi dan vektor Blochnya berputar stabil dari kutub ke kutub &mdash; ia **bernutasi**. Jika kita menerapkan rotasi dengan flip angle $\\theta$ mengelilingi sumbu-$x$ pada qubit yang mulai dari $|0\\rangle$, probabilitas menemukannya di $|1\\rangle$ adalah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$P_1(\\theta) = \\sin^2\\!\\left(\\tfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\bigl(1 - \\cos\\theta\\bigr).$$\n"
msgstr "$$P_1(\\theta) = \\sin^2\\!\\left(\\tfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\bigl(1 - \\cos\\theta\\bigr).$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the **Rabi curve**. Its first maximum is the $\\pi$ pulse (full inversion, the $180^\\circ$ pulse); a $\\pi/2$ pulse is a quarter-turn (the $90^\\circ$ pulse that tips a spin into the transverse plane). In NMR this curve is how you *calibrate* your pulses.\n"
msgstr "Inilah **kurva Rabi**. Maksimum pertamanya adalah pulsa $\\pi$ (inversi penuh, pulsa $180^\\circ$); pulsa $\\pi/2$ adalah seperempat putaran (pulsa $90^\\circ$ yang memiringkan spin ke bidang transversal). Dalam NMR, kurva ini adalah cara kamu *mengkalibrasi* pulsa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Experimental caveat\">\n"
"A *literal* Rabi experiment sweeps the drive amplitude or duration in time. That requires pulse-level control, which was removed in Qiskit v2.0. Here we instead sweep the **rotation angle** $\\theta$ of an $R_X(\\theta)$ gate. The curve and the $\\pi$/$\\pi/2$ identification are identical; the only difference is that we choose an angle directly instead of calibrating a pulse length. On hardware with *fractional gates*, $R_X(\\theta)$ for arbitrary $\\theta$ runs natively.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan eksperimen\">\n"
"Eksperimen Rabi yang *sebenarnya* menyapu amplitudo atau durasi drive terhadap waktu. Itu membutuhkan kontrol tingkat pulsa, yang dihapus di Qiskit v2.0. Di sini kita justru menyapu **sudut rotasi** $\\theta$ dari gate $R_X(\\theta)$. Kurvanya dan identifikasi $\\pi$/$\\pi/2$ identik; satu-satunya perbedaan adalah kita memilih sudut secara langsung, bukan mengkalibrasi panjang pulsa. Pada hardware dengan *fractional gate*, $R_X(\\theta)$ untuk $\\theta$ sembarang berjalan secara native.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

